<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Madosa Q1 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Madosa Q1 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period ended Dec 27, 1996.</p>
<p>Shr loss 6.65 bolivars vs profit 26.62 bolivar</p>
<p>Net loss 153 million bolivars vs profit 614 million profit</p>
<p>Sales 9.1 bln bolivars vs 6.4 bln bolivars</p>
<p>Cost of sales 7.6 bln bolivars vs 4.7 bln bolivars</p>
<p>Operational costs 1.2 bln bolivars vs 717 million bolivars</p>
<p>NOTES: Madosa is a domestic appliances manufacturer.</p>
<p>Results are inflation adjusted in constant 1996 bolivars.</p>
<p>Enron Corp holds a 42 percent share in Madosa.</p>
<p>General Electric Co holds 34 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
